---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const terms = [
  ['Signal', 'A bounded material change that passed the publication gate. A Signal is not a complete news item or a claim that the change applies everywhere.'],
  ['Thread', 'A maintained thesis that connects material changes over time. Threads can strengthen, stay unchanged, weaken, become inconclusive, or be falsified as evidence changes.'],
  ['Falsifier', 'A concrete observation that would weaken or overturn the current judgment. Falsifiers are conditions to watch, not predictions that GrepSignal expects to happen.'],
  ['Limitation', 'A known boundary on what the evidence supports. A limitation narrows the claim; it is not boilerplate legal caution.'],
  ['Watch next', 'The observations that would be most useful for updating the judgment. It is a monitoring agenda, not a generic recommendation.'],
  ['Prediction', 'A separately registered, time-bounded and falsifiable claim with fixed resolution criteria. GrepSignal does not create one merely to fill the ledger.'],
  ['Lifecycle', 'Whether a record is active, superseded, or retracted. Lifecycle is separate from the judgment assessment such as strengthening or weakening.'],
  ['Revision', 'An accepted material change to a published judgment. Cosmetic presentation changes are not revisions.'],
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How to read GrepSignal"
  description="A human guide to Signals, Threads, falsifiers, limitations, predictions, and GrepSignal's evidence and revision conventions."
>
  <main class="wrap reading-guide">
    <header class="guide-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">&gt; help --read-grepsignal</div>
      <h1>How to read GrepSignal.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        GrepSignal is a maintained judgment layer, not a news feed. Start with what changed, then read why it matters,
        what would change the view, and where the evidence came from.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="quick-read" aria-labelledby="quick-read-title">
      <span class="section-kicker">30-SECOND VERSION</span>
      <h2 id="quick-read-title">Read the judgment before the machinery.</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Signal:</strong> What materially changed?</li>
        <li><strong>Why it matters:</strong> What should a technical builder update in their mental model?</li>
        <li><strong>Second-order effect:</strong> What could change one step downstream?</li>
        <li><strong>Watch next:</strong> What evidence would make the judgment move?</li>
        <li><strong>Falsifiers + limitations:</strong> Where could this be wrong or overgeneralized?</li>
        <li><strong>Sources:</strong> Trace important claims back to the linked evidence.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="terms-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="section-kicker">GLOSSARY</span>
        <h2 id="terms-title">The terms GrepSignal uses.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="term-list">
        {terms.map(([term, definition]) => (
          <article>
            <h3>{term}</h3>
            <p>{definition}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="interpretation-grid" aria-label="How to interpret GrepSignal records">
      <article>
        <span class="section-kicker">STATUS</span>
        <h2>Strengthening is not a confidence score.</h2>
        <p>
          <code>emerging</code>, <code>strengthening</code>, <code>stable</code>, <code>weakening</code>, and <code>falsified</code>
          describe how the tracked judgment is moving. They are not probabilities and there is no target distribution across statuses.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="section-kicker">ABSENCE</span>
        <h2>Not published does not mean unimportant.</h2>
        <p>
          An event may be unreviewed, out of scope, below the materiality threshold, deferred, or still under watch.
          GrepSignal intentionally allows zero new Signals.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="section-kicker">DATES</span>
        <h2>Registration is not the event date.</h2>
        <p>
          GrepSignal keeps registration, observation, source publication, retrieval, review, and public-publication times separate.
          Unknown historical timestamps remain unknown rather than being reconstructed.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="section-kicker">SOURCES</span>
        <h2>More URLs do not automatically mean more evidence.</h2>
        <p>
          Vendor sources can establish narrow facts about their own products. General performance, adoption, or causal claims need
          evidence appropriate to those claims. Several articles repeating one announcement are still one evidence lineage.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="trust-section">
      <span class="section-kicker">TRUST MODEL</span>
      <h2>What to trust, and what not to.</h2>
      <p>
        Treat the published Signal or Thread as GrepSignal's current editorial judgment. Treat linked evidence as the basis for
        checking important claims. Local AI explanations are optional reading aids and cannot change the canonical record.
        The Changes journal shows accepted revisions and reviews when judgments move.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a href={`${base}signals/`}>Browse Signals →</a>
        <a href={`${base}threads/`}>Browse Threads →</a>
        <a href={`${base}changes/`}>See judgment changes →</a>
        <a href={`${base}editorial/`}>Read the editorial policy →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .reading-guide { max-width: 1040px; padding-top: 66px; padding-bottom: 90px; }
  .guide-hero { max-width: 880px; padding-bottom: 44px; }
  .guide-hero h1 { margin: 9px 0 20px; font-size: clamp(48px, 7vw, 82px); }
  .lead { max-width: 820px; margin: 0; color: #383733; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .quick-read, .trust-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); padding-top: 27px; margin-top: 18px; }
  h2 { margin: 6px 0 16px; font: 600 31px/1.12 Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .quick-read ol { max-width: 840px; margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; }
  .quick-read li { padding: 9px 0; line-height: 1.6; }
  .section-heading { margin-top: 58px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .term-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .term-list article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 170px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .term-list h3 { margin: 0; font: 650 21px Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
  .term-list p { max-width: 760px; margin: 0; color: #3b3a36; line-height: 1.65; }
  .interpretation-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 26px; margin-top: 58px; }
  .interpretation-grid article { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--panel); padding: 26px; }
  .interpretation-grid h2 { font-size: 25px; }
  .interpretation-grid p, .trust-section p { color: #3b3a36; line-height: 1.7; }
  .interpretation-grid code { font-size: .9em; }
  .trust-section { margin-top: 58px; }
  .trust-section p { max-width: 820px; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 22px; margin-top: 22px; }
  .actions a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 750; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .reading-guide { padding-top: 46px; }
    .lead { font-size: 18px; }
    .term-list article, .interpretation-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .term-list article { gap: 8px; }
  }
</style>
